ds. theme_plan has the corresponding contiguous theme_1 through theme_k, each exactly topic,principle,conditions,consequences,fact_ids. principle is a string <= 600 characters. conditions and consequences are JSON arrays of 0-7 nonempty strings, each <= 240 characters; use [] when absent. fact_ids is an array of provided ID strings. The point topic and its corresponding theme topic must be identical. Plan all parts together first, then write one point per theme. A fact ID has one primary theme owner; overview facts already carried by summary need not create another point. fact_ids are ownership/association hints, not final citations; the caller derives actual references. Use only provided IDs, never guess. Unused trailing slots may be omitted/null. Do not emit key_points as a second representation. Theme metadata is not proof of support."
